{
  "source": "experiments/plot_tradeoff.py, from docs/value-propagation/results and tuning",
  "conventions": {
    "share": "A, B: share of a method's 210 final runs (the four maze sets pooled) whose frozen greedy route is a shortest route at x real steps or x Q-value updates. A run's state at x is its check after the last episode that ended within x: not shortest before its first episode ends, and its final state carried forward once it has finished its 1,000 episodes. Intervals: 95% Wilson.",
    "first_reaches_half": "A, B: the smallest x at which the pooled share is at least 50%, exact over every episode end; at_half gives Q-learning's x over the method's (real steps) and the method's over Q-learning's (updates).",
    "updates_to_converge": "Q-value updates (real, trace and planning) summed through the converged episode, as analysis.json counts them.",
    "paired": "C: suite mazes; geometric means over the mazes on which both methods converged, real steps as Q-learning's over the method's and updates as the method's over Q-learning's, with 95% percentile-bootstrap intervals (the same numbers as analysis.json).",
    "development": "D: development mazes (seeds 1000-1019 of each type), not the final runs. Each axis is a separate median over the configuration's runs, a run that did not converge counted as +inf (null: not reached).",
    "dominance": "D: a configuration dominates another if it converged on at least as many runs, with no more median real steps and no more median updates to convergence, and strictly better in at least one of the three. non_dominated: non-dominated among the 15 measured configurations, not a Pareto frontier.",
    "agent_time": "E: wall-clock seconds inside agent calls per 1,000-episode run, median and interquartile range (numpy percentiles, linear interpolation). Indicative: measured with concurrent worker processes on one hybrid-core laptop CPU, not a controlled benchmark."
  },
